"""Practical, first-principles descriptions for FringeScope controls."""
SOURCES={
 'mirror':('Mirror motion','wobble','Residual mirror motion changes optical path difference by twice the mirror displacement. The detector responds according to the local interferogram slope and phase. The default is a biased 840 Hz sinusoid; composite shapes are optional settings within this same mechanism.'),
 'globar':('Globar leakage','globar','Continuous out-of-band thermal-source light passes insufficient filtering and folds on the OPD grid. Stable leakage enters both reference and signal and can dilute a real difference spectrum. It does not create a flash transient in a stationary linear system.'),
 'laser':('532 nm actinic leakage','laser','A small part of the excitation pulse reaches the detector at the flash. Its temporal response is integrated over recorder bins. An OPD-modulated return can alias at the optical wavelength; direct bypass light has no such spatial carrier.')}

TIPS={
 'electrical':'Additive electrical pickup in the detector chain. Its temporal frequency and phase are independent of mirror motion. A 60 Hz harmonic is a possible source, not an identification of the observed oscillation.',
 'zpd':'A differential return-position or registration mismatch between reference and postflash records. It changes sampled optical phase, but a constant mismatch alone is not a temporal oscillation.',
 'mirror_nm':'Peak amplitude of the fundamental mirror drive, in nm. OPD changes by twice this displacement. Added harmonics can make the total excursion larger.',
 'frequency_hz':'Mechanical drive frequency in Hz. 840 Hz gives a 1.19 ms period. This is a sensitivity hypothesis, not a measured mirror resonance.',
 'phase_deg':'Timing phase of the mirror oscillation relative to the flash, in degrees. It moves maxima in time; it is different from a common position/phase bias.',
 'bias_nm':'Common mirror registration offset, applied to both reference and signal. Together with motion and fixed-phase reconstruction it can produce a fundamental-frequency artifact rather than a predominantly doubled-frequency response.',
 'waveform':'Choose the displacement waveform within the single Mirror motion mechanism. Composite modes add harmonics or an envelope; they are not another independent artifact source.',
 'second_ratio':'Amplitude of the 2f displacement term divided by the fundamental amplitude. Nonlinear optical readout can also generate 2f even when this setting is zero.',
 'third_ratio':'Amplitude of the 3f displacement term divided by the fundamental. Used by the three-harmonic, servo and envelope modes.',
 'second_phase_deg':'Phase of the 2f displacement term relative to twice the fundamental phase, in degrees.',
 'third_phase_deg':'Phase of the 3f displacement term relative to three times the fundamental phase, in degrees.',
 'chirp_hz_per_ms':'Linear frequency drift of the mechanical drive in Hz per millisecond. Zero gives a stationary carrier.',
 'envelope_slope':'Linear amplitude-envelope slope across the acquisition window. Zero gives constant amplitude; this is an assumed waveform, not measured motion.',
 'quadrature_slope':'Linear envelope on the quadrature component. It permits a changing waveform phase/envelope without declaring an additional physical oscillator.',
 'servo_fraction':'Strength of a smooth step-like displacement contribution, relative to the fundamental. Used only by the servo-like waveform preset.',
 'phase_mode':'Trigger locked repeats the same disturbance each shot. Random changes phase for each step/shot. Free running continues through preflash and follows an assumed scan schedule.',
 'coadds':'Shots averaged per OPD position. Trigger-locked disturbances repeat coherently and do not automatically decrease as 1/sqrt(N).',
 'repetition_hz':'Flash repetition rate used in the assumed free-running acquisition schedule. It controls sampled phase relationships, not the chemical decay constants.',
 'settle_ms':'Assumed waiting time after changing OPD position, used for free-running phase accumulation. It is not an added delay in the displayed kinetics.',
 'globar_fraction':'Peak of the deposited folded thermal-source spectrum before blocking, in the model reference spectrum’s relative units. This is a detector-equivalent sensitivity setting, not measured optical power.',
 'blocking_od':'Optical density suppressing thermal leakage. Each unit attenuates the modeled leak by a factor of ten.',
 'leak_center':'Center of an assumed out-of-band Gaussian transmission leak in cm⁻¹. It multiplies the thermal-source spectrum before spatial folding.',
 'leak_width':'Standard deviation of the assumed transmission leak in cm⁻¹. This is spectral filtering, not the temporal width of a flash.',
 'leak_transient_ppm':'Optional change in otherwise continuous thermal leakage after the flash, in parts per million. Zero is stable leakage; a nonzero value explicitly introduces a separate transient assumption.',
 'laser_area_us':'Integrated detector-equivalent pulse area divided by reference IFG peak, in µs. It scales the applied pulse; it does not change the optical alias location.',
 'laser_blocking_od':'Optical density blocking the 532 nm pulse. Each unit reduces its applied amplitude tenfold.',
 'laser_route':'OPD-modulated return carries optical interference fringes. Uniform direct bypass is independent of OPD. Step-dependent bypass creates a different spectrum from its coupling pattern, not from optical wavelength.',
 'pulse_fwhm_ns':'Optical pulse FWHM before the detector response. The nominal 6 ns pulse is much shorter than the default 6 µs recorder bin.',
 'reflection_ns':'Assumed exponential optical-delay tail, in ns. A 20 ns free-space delay corresponds to about 6 m of extra path; small reflections alone do not establish that delay.',
 'response_us':'Assumed first-order detector/electronics response time in µs, convolved with the optical pulse. This is not a calibrated visible-light detector response.',
 'laser_delay_us':'Pulse timing relative to the flash/bin boundaries. It can redistribute pulse area between neighboring bins.',
 'hene_fraction':'Continuous detector-equivalent HeNe IFG level divided by the ideal IR reference IFG peak. The interferometric branch is level × [1 + cos(optical phase)]. It is present in both reference and signal.',
 'hene_blocking_od':'Optical density blocking the continuous HeNe contribution. Each unit attenuates it tenfold; no flash gating is introduced.',
 'hene_nm':'Nominal HeNe wavelength in nm. The default is 632.8 nm. The true air/vacuum wavelength and OPD sampling relation require setup verification because the alias lies close to a band boundary.',
 'hene_route':'An OPD-modulated return has a wavelength-dependent carrier and is displaced by the same assumed mirror motion. Uniform direct leakage adds a constant detector term with no optical-wavelength alias.',
 'hene_phase_deg':'Static optical phase of the HeNe path. This is separate from temporal mirror phase and is not a fitted instrument calibration.',
 'return_nm':'Differential mirror-position offset after the flash, in nm. It represents a registration mismatch, not an independent 840 Hz oscillator.',
 'jitter_nm':'Standard deviation of a fixed per-OPD-step return error, in nm. The deterministic seed is exported; this is distinct from a repeated sinusoidal drive.',
 'electrical_fraction':'Additive electrical detector pickup relative to the reference IFG peak. Unlike mirror motion it does not require optical displacement.',
 'electrical_frequency':'Frequency for the independent additive electrical pickup when Free frequency is selected.',
 'electrical_phase_deg':'Electrical pickup phase relative to the flash. It is independent of the mirror phase control.',
 'electrical_mode':'Choose an integer multiple of nominal 60 Hz mains, or an independently specified frequency. Matching 14 × 60 = 840 Hz does not establish an electrical cause.',
 'mains_harmonic':'Integer harmonic of nominal 60 Hz mains. Fourteen gives 840 Hz. This is an illustrative hypothesis, not measured mains coupling.',
 'heat_tau':'Lifetime of the synthetic heating-like exponential, in µs. Gaussian component amplitudes retain their signs; the component assignment is a model assumption.',
 'rp_tau':'Lifetime of the synthetic recombination-like exponential, in µs. This model parameter is not a new measured PSI recombination lifetime.',
 'heat_scale':'Multiplier of the fast heating-like exponential H only. The unresolved offset C has its own scale and includes a declared heating-like fraction. This is not per-spectrum normalization.',
 'rp_scale':'Multiplier of the decaying PSI component R only. The separately scaled unresolved offset includes a declared residual PSI fraction; these are illustrative amplitudes, not measured populations.',
 'offset_scale':'Multiplier of the causal unresolved component C = 0.08 R + 0.04 H. The fractions are illustrative, not calibrated yields or temperatures. This changes input data; the Fit non-decaying offset checkbox only changes the fitted basis.',
 'fit_start':'Start of the time window used for unweighted lifetime optimization and projection diagnostics, in µs.',
 'fit_stop':'End of the fit time window in µs. A lifetime longer than the selected window may not be independently resolved.',
 'fit_low':'Low-wavenumber bound of the lifetime-optimization region. The selected lifetimes are projected at all finite valid spectral channels.',
 'fit_high':'High-wavenumber bound of the lifetime-optimization region, in cm⁻¹. The display remains full-band.',
 'phase_readout':'Fixed-phase real reconstruction is sensitive to phase/registration errors. Magnitude is a separate sensitivity comparison, not an implementation of the instrument phase correction.',
}
